# Security Guidelines for Escape Room Game

## Input Validation & Sanitization

- Validate all user inputs on both client and server side
- Sanitize puzzle answers before comparison (case-sensitive matching)
- Prevent XSS attacks by properly escaping user-generated content
- Validate room IDs to prevent unauthorized access to rooms

## Session Security

- Store sensitive session data in secure HTTP-only cookies when possible
- Use localStorage for non-sensitive game state only
- Implement proper session timeout mechanisms
- Validate player progression to prevent room skipping

## API Security

- Use HTTPS for all API communications
- Implement rate limiting for API endpoints
- Validate API responses before processing
- Use environment variables for sensitive configuration (NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL)

## Data Protection

- Hash or encrypt sensitive player data in Redis
- Implement proper CORS policies
- Use Content Security Policy (CSP) headers
- Sanitize error messages to prevent information disclosure

## Game Logic Security

- Server-side validation of puzzle answers
- Prevent client-side manipulation of game state
- Implement anti-cheat measures for leaderboard
- Validate hint usage and room completion status

## File Upload Security (if applicable)

- Validate file types and sizes for any image uploads
- Scan uploaded files for malware
- Store uploaded files outside web root
- Use secure file naming conventions
